 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`Pullback/Smooth.lean:272` has only the bundled `mpullback_comp : mpullback (g \u2218 f) _ = (mpullback f hf).comp (mpullback g hg)`. A grep for `theorem mpullback_mpullback` finds only the new `_symm` variants, so there is no pointwise form, which is why each call site has to fold through `LinearMap.comp_apply` by hand.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/GroupAction/InvariantForm.lean",
   "fix": "Add a pointwise lemma to `Pullback/Smooth.lean`: `SmoothForm.mpullback_mpullback (f) (g) (hf) (hg) (\u03b2) : mpullback f hf (mpullback g hg \u03b2) = mpullback (g \u2218 f) (hg.comp hf) \u03b2`. Rewrite with it at every site above. The private `mpullback_quotientMk_comp_objectDiffeomorph` then becomes an instance of it and can be dropped.",
   "issue": "`mpullback_objectDiffeomorph_mem_invariantForms_iff` uses the rewrite pair `\u2190 LinearMap.comp_apply, \u2190 SmoothForm.mpullback_comp` twice to merge nested pullbacks. The same pair appears in `mpullback_map_obj_mem_invariantForms` (both calc steps, lines ~224 and ~230) and in `mpullback_quotientMk_mem_invariantForms` (~line 317). `invariantForms.mpullback_comp` and the private `mpullback_quotientMk_comp_objectDiffeomorph` do the same thing through `LinearMap.congr_fun (SmoothForm.mpullback_comp \u2026)`. The underlying fact is never stated as its own lemma.",
   "line": 146
  }
 ],
